
"smart_sources:- Record of Decision - Craters Of The Moon National Monument & Preserve (U.S. National Park Service).md": {"path":"- Record of Decision - Craters Of The Moon National Monument & Preserve (U.S. National Park Service).md","last_embed":{"hash":null},"embeddings":{},"last_read":{"hash":"1i2jiif","at":1785794992490},"class_name":"SmartSource","last_import":{"mtime":1785183079036,"size":41358,"at":1785794992780,"hash":"1i2jiif"},"blocks":{"#---frontmatter---":[1,8],"#":[9,234],"###Natural Resources":[235,236],"###Geological Resources and Caves":[237,240],"###Geological Resources and Caves#{1}":[239,240],"###Soils and Water":[241,248],"###Soils and Water#{1}":[243,248],"###Vegetation, including Special Status Species, and Fire Management":[249,258],"###Vegetation, including Special Status Species, and Fire Management#{1}":[251,258],"###Wildlife and Special Status Species":[259,260],"###A variety of techniques would be employed to reduce the impacts on wildlife, such as visitor education programs and restrictions on visitor activities. NPS, in conjunction with the State of Idaho, would designate areas within the Preserve and periods of time when no hunting would be permitted for reasons of public safety, protection of the areas’ resources, administration, or public use and enjoyment.":[261,264],"###A variety of techniques would be employed to reduce the impacts on wildlife, such as visitor education programs and restrictions on visitor activities. NPS, in conjunction with the State of Idaho, would designate areas within the Preserve and periods of time when no hunting would be permitted for reasons of public safety, protection of the areas’ resources, administration, or public use and enjoyment.#{1}":[263,264],"###Air Quality":[265,268],"###Air Quality#{1}":[267,268],"###Cultural Resources":[269,285],"###Cultural Resources#{1}":[271,285]},"outlinks":[{"title":"Idaho","target":"Idaho","line":11}],"metadata":{"title":"Record of Decision - Craters Of The Moon N